May I suggest another way of dealing with this problem, borrowed from
moria.

In moria, there are (I speak from memory) the Oozes. These Oozes divide
when you hit them, and when you finally kill them, they leave a number
of items. To make sure that you don't get unlimited items or Oozes,
these monsters move erratically, and when doing so, they have a chance
of eating eachother, thus reducing their number.

Their erratic movement is gravitating towards you, so eventually, they
will all move in your direction, speeding up the process of them
colliding and reducing their numbers even more.

Of course, in moria, there is another thing limiting the number of
items. In that game, you can only carry a limited number of items (bags
do not exist). So even if you managed to generate 20 holy avengers, 10
defenders, and a hundred rings of free action, you still wouldn't be
able to take them all with you.

